<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Defs>
  <!--
    The adrenaline shot's effect, MDWC_Adrenaline since a DefOf field is named by its def and
    the ability already holds MDWC_AdrenalineShot (Ability_AdrenalineShot applies it; design in
    Docs/Specs/Adrenaline-Shot.md 3.2): go-juice's high (Core, Drugs/GoJuice.xml) on a short
    clock, with no tolerance and no addiction, pure XML. Hediff_High is go-juice's class and only
    shows the severity as a percentage. The shot sets severity 1, and severityPerDay -8 fades it
    in three hours: the top three stages' thirds are its boost levels of an hour each, and the
    bottom twelfth (wearing off's minSeverity 0.084) is the crash, the last quarter hour. The
    duration is a mod setting written onto severityPerDay, which scales every level with it (a
    shot already given keeps the rate it was applied with, since vanilla's comp caches it per
    instance). A second shot refreshes the severity rather than adding to it, so a patient is
    never above 1, and a crashing patient can be shot straight back to the rush.

    Stages are listed ascending by minSeverity as vanilla requires, so the top level is last.
    The rush is go-juice's stage verbatim; the next two taper its offsets by thirds. The crash
    is the one cost the player feels, since rest is paid invisibly: small negative
    Consciousness and Moving offsets and no pain relief, landing long after most fights end, so
    it taxes the afternoon rather than the fight. The comedown is each stage's
    restFallFactor, vanilla's own lever, climbing a step per level so the bill rises as the
    boost thins, the crash the top rung: a full shot costs about 0.25 of rest beyond what three
    waking hours cost anyway, paid continuously while awake and not at all asleep, and read
    live, so the setting that writes the top stage's factor (each lower stage one higher)
    reaches shots already running. The pilot's own RestFallRateFactor multiplies on top.

    everCurableByItem false: a healer mech serum must not spend itself on a stimulant. No
    scenarioCanAdd: it is the shoulders' to give. Under Combat Extended the boost levels also
    carry go-juice's suppression resistance (1.6/Mods/CombatExtended/Patches/
    AdrenalineSuppression.xml, by stage label).
  -->
  <HediffDef>
    <defName>MDWC_Adrenaline</defName>
    <hediffClass>Hediff_High</hediffClass>
    <label>adrenaline shot</label>
    <labelNoun>an adrenaline shot</labelNoun>
    <description>A shot of adrenaline, fading in levels. Pain is dulled and movement, sight and thought are quickened, while the body burns through its sleep faster and faster as the surge fades, and a short crash follows.</description>
    <defaultLabelColor>(1,0,0.5)</defaultLabelColor>
    <isBad>false</isBad>
    <everCurableByItem>false</everCurableByItem>
    <initialSeverity>1</initialSeverity>
    <maxSeverity>1</maxSeverity>
    <comps>
      <li Class="HediffCompProperties_SeverityPerDay">
        <severityPerDay>-8</severityPerDay>
        <showHoursToRecover>true</showHoursToRecover>
      </li>
    </comps>
    <stages>
      <li>
        <label>crash</label>
        <restFallFactor>5</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>-0.10</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>wearing off</label>
        <minSeverity>0.084</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.7</painFactor>
        <restFallFactor>4</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.07</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Sight</capacity>
            <offset>0.12</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.17</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>fading</label>
        <minSeverity>0.334</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.4</painFactor>
        <restFallFactor>3</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.13</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Sight</capacity>
            <offset>0.23</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.33</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>rush</label>
        <minSeverity>0.667</minSeverity>
        <painFactor>0.1</painFactor>
        <restFallFactor>2</restFallFactor>
        <capMods>
          <li>
            <capacity>Consciousness</capacity>
            <offset>0.20</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Sight</capacity>
            <offset>0.35</offset>
          </li>
          <li>
            <capacity>Moving</capacity>
            <offset>0.50</offset>
          </li>
        </capMods>
      </li>
    </stages>
  </HediffDef>
</Defs>
